.TH UCABLED 1 "2026-10-13" "ucabled" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ucabled \- virtual FIDO2 device that relays WebAuthn to a phone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ucabled
.RB [ \-\-no\-ui ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ucabled
creates a virtual FIDO2/U2F HID device through the kernel's
.B /dev/uhid
interface and relays each WebAuthn ceremony to a phone over the caBLE v2
hybrid transport (the same QR\-then\-Bluetooth flow browsers use).
It normally runs as a systemd system service and is triggered by the kernel
on behalf of a client, so it is not meant to be run by hand.
.PP
When a ceremony starts, the daemon asks the per\-user
.BR ucable\-agent (1)
to show a QR code window; the user scans it with their phone and confirms
the request there.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ui
Print the QR code on the terminal instead of asking the session agent.
Useful on machines without a graphical session.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter, defaulting to
.BR info .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dist/ucabled.service
The systemd unit that runs the daemon as the
.I ucabled
service account.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ucable\-agent (1),
.BR ucable\-agent\-helper (1)
